                <pb facs="0456" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">452.11/201</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Padilla</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75–11</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Referring to Your Excellency’s
                    kind note dated November 7 last<anchor n="4" xml:id="d280-f1"/> relative to the
                    recognition on the part of the Government of the United States of North America
                    of the Spanish protectorate zone in Morocco and remembering the statements made
                    therein it behooves me to say to Your Excellency that the Government of His
                    Majesty has sent to its Consul General at Tangier the proper instructions for
                    him to come to an agreement with the Diplomatic Agent and Consul General of the
                    United States there in order to arrive at an early and full settlement of the
                    claims of North American subjects, originating in the Protectorate zone which
                    are still awaiting decision. This favorable inclination of the Government of His
                    Majesty wholly meets the wishes expressed by that of the United States of which
                    Your Excellency is so worthy a part and therefore it is to be hoped that the
                    action entrusted to the representatives of both high parties in Tangiers will
                    bring about the desired solution.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alejandro Padilla</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
